# ── LocalWheels Frontend — Environment Variables ─────────────────────────────

# ── Clerk Authentication ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Required for Clerk auth UI (SignIn, SignUp, UserButton).
#   Get from: https://dashboard.clerk.com → Your App → API Keys → Publishable key
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# Copy instructions differ by deployment target — see below.
# NEVER commit a real .env file; only this .env.example is committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   DO NOT create a .env.local file for development.
#   Vite's dev proxy (vite.config.js) forwards /api/* → localhost:5000
#   automatically, so VITE_API_URL is not needed locally.

# ── Production: Vercel + Render ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#   In the Vercel dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables, add:
#     VITE_API_URL = https://localwheels-backend.onrender.com/api
#
#   Then redeploy. The frontend will call the Render backend directly.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://localwheels-backend.onrender.com/api

# ── Production: VPS (nginx reverse-proxy — RECOMMENDED) ──────────────────────
#   If nginx on your VPS proxies /api → backend (see docs/nginx.conf),
#   you do NOT need to set VITE_API_URL at all. The built app falls back
#   to the relative /api path, which nginx routes to your backend.
#
#   Steps:
#     1. npm run build           (no .env file needed — uses /api fallback)
#     2. Deploy dist/ to /var/www/localwheels/dist
#     3. Apply docs/nginx.conf   (handles SPA routing + API proxy)
#
#   If your backend runs on a DIFFERENT domain from the frontend:
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com/api

# ── Production: Hostinger / cPanel shared hosting ─────────────────────────────
#   Shared hosting cannot run a Node.js backend. Use Render (free tier) for
#   the backend and Hostinger for the frontend only.
#
#   Steps:
#     1. Create a .env.production file (gitignored) with:
#          VITE_API_URL=https://localwheels-backend.onrender.com/api
#     2. Run: npm run build
#            (Vite automatically picks up .env.production during build)
#     3. Upload the entire contents of dist/ to your Hostinger public_html/ folder.
#        The .htaccess file in dist/ (copied from public/.htaccess) handles
#        SPA routing so page refreshes and direct links work correctly.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://localwheels-backend.onrender.com/api
